From e6026418366c2f6232bdd39d2d15f4aeb46184c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:57:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] leds: flash: Support first-generation Qualcomm PMIC torch
 mode

Refresh cbfe7bb0e361, originally by Timothy Schmidt with Claude Opus 5.5
assistance. Preserve the register sequence already exercised on PM8226
in the existing Fx0 integration. This is new support on the LED
maintainer base, not a mainline regression fix.

A source-extracted host fixture reproduces five shutdown fault cases in
the carried implementation. Attempt the remaining off operations after a
register error and retain the supply reference if disable fails.

All five cases, eight on-error controls, 32 healthy brightness cases and
400 concurrent callback transactions pass under ASan/UBSan. Both native
ARM and ARM64 objects compile without warnings. Current-base hardware,
boost, flash strobe and limits remain unqualified.

Refreshed with OpenAI Codex assistance; human review and DCO pending.
